*not* divisible by $9.$ So, $9\\,173\\,589$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $733\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+3+1+2+3=19,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $733\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223365" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $448$\n\nII. $352$\n\nIII. $217$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0e5ee54-f96c-54ab-8de5-f272c76ac6c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432795 #edb/ref 1074 "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $448,$ we have that \n\n$$\n44-2(8)=44-16=28\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $448$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $352,$ we have that \n\n$$\n35-2(2)=35-4=31\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $352$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $217,$ we have that \n\n$$\n21-2(7)=21-14=7\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $217$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223456" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $476$\n\nII. $732$\n\nIII. $423$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fdf659d7-2ff6-5274-9913-97ffa0cf4e09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432796 #edb/ref 1074 "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $476,$ we have that \n\n$$\n47-2(6)=47-12=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $476$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $732,$ we have that \n\n$$\n73-2(2)=73-4=69\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $732$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $423,$ we have that \n\n$$\n42-2(3)=42-6=36\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $423$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
